#!/usr/bin/env python3
# exercise-enter -- deterministic per-EXERCISE-ENTRY forcing point (the
# sibling of session-open: session-open is the deterministic SESSION-birth
# chokepoint, exercise-enter is the deterministic EXERCISE-entry chokepoint).
#
# WHY (root fix -- closes batch #13, #14, #21, #28, all clustered at "exercise
# entry"):
#   Every exercise entry must PRE-EMPTIVELY deliver, from state, the same four
#   things that kept getting dropped under live pressure because they were
#   MODEL-DRIVEN (prompt discipline is not a reliable carrier -- D2):
#     #13 set-table (표2) dropped on entry. The entry-time (2) progress-table
#         publish was model-driven; complex entries (JIT equipment reg + prep
#         drills, e.g. v_squat) swallowed it, and the only net -- set-add's
#         SET_TABLE_MISSING -- fires at the first WORKING set (after warmup),
#         so the table could be missing through the whole warmup. FIX: entry
#         publish becomes STRUCTURAL -- exercise-enter renders the (2) table at
#         entry, before warmup/cues, and drops set-table's own published flag
#         so the set-add fallback stays consistent.
#     #14 exercise card (표3) not dashboard-pinned. 표3=대시보드 핀 고정,
#         표2=인라인 흐름 (owner memory). The pin capability ALREADY exists:
#         bridge/dashboard.py (DGN-214) mirrors <bot_data_dir>/dashboard.md
#         into ONE pinned owner-chat message and keeps the pin alive. The
#         generator owns the file's content; the bridge is a dumb watch+sync.
#         So this is a pack-side dashboard.md wiring, NOT a framework seam:
#         exercise-enter renders the 표3 card and WRITES it to the dashboard.md
#         pin surface, and the bridge auto-pins+syncs it. (The earlier
#         "PIN_REQUEST -> framework" path was a mis-diagnosis -- a subagent grep'd
#         only push.sh and missed dashboard.py's pin capability.)
#     #21 entry cue missing confirmed settings (grip etc.). the user had to ask
#         "그립 뭘로하냐". The confirmed, UNCHANGING per-exercise settings that
#         already exist in records (grip / setup / loading side) must be
#         surfaced PRE-EMPTIVELY at entry -- never make the user ask.
#     #28 re-asking a param that is in records -- the user pushed back on
#         being asked for something already on file.
#         (weak-side was already recorded). Record-backed params (weak side,
#         unilateral order) must be AUTO-LOADED, never re-asked.
#
# WHAT (fired at every exercise entry; idempotent; best-effort):
#   (a) publish the (2) set-table [#13] by REUSING set-table.render (no
#       reimplementation) and marking set-table's own published flag.
#   (b) render the (3) exercise card [#14] and WRITE it to the dashboard.md pin
#       surface (bridge/dashboard.py auto-pins+syncs it). Best-effort: a write
#       failure never breaks the entry.
#   (c) surface CONFIRMED_SETTINGS from records [#21] -- grip / setup cue /
#       loading side, read straight from the program.yaml slot (the SoT for
#       per-exercise settings; DB grip tables are muscle-decomposition, not
#       user-facing cues).
#   (d) auto-load RECORD_PARAMS [#28] -- weak-side / unilateral order detected
#       from the slot's safety_note + last-result prose, so nothing recorded is
#       re-asked.
#   (e) surface the PRIOR-ACTUAL anchor [#43] -- the weight the owner ACTUALLY
#       worked last time they did THIS exercise, read from workout_sets, so the
#       cue frames "직전 N kg -> 오늘 M kg" deterministically instead of a bare
#       weight surprise ("싱글레그 왜 40키로냐"). First-ever -> "첫 기록".
#   All of (b)-(d) are emitted as MACHINE LINES the model echoes (exactly like
#   session-open's OPENED line / set-add's NEXT_HINT), so the model does not
#   have to REMEMBER to provide them -- it reads them off the deterministic
#   output.
#
# Idempotency + live-safety (this is the HOT entry path):
#   - A per-(session, exercise) entered-marker makes re-entry cheap and
#     non-spammy: a second call prints ENTERED_ALREADY and STILL re-emits the
#     confirmed settings + params (they are read-only reads, never a re-ask),
#     but does not re-publish a duplicate set-table push order.
#   - BEST-EFFORT throughout: any single section failing (set-table render,
#     card render, settings read) prints a WARN to stderr and the entry
#     PROCEEDS. exercise-enter must NEVER break an exercise entry.
#   - No writes to workout rows/sets. The only side effects are two marker
#     files (this script's entered-marker + set-table's published flag), both
#     best-effort.
#
# Usage:
#   exercise-enter <session_id> <exercise_name>
#       [--db PATH] [--program PATH] [--force] [--no-table]
#     --force        : re-publish even if already entered (correction re-entry).
#     --no-table     : skip the (2) table publish (settings/params only).
#   exercise-enter <session_id> <exercise_name> --refresh-card
#     the 표3 pin refresh, fired on every set-add success.
#   exercise-enter <session_id> <exercise_name> --publish-table
#     the 표2 PER-SET beat, fired on every set-add success. Renders the table
#     from live state and DELIVERS it (do_publish_table). Same F14 gate, same
#     content-signature delivery ledger as the entry publish above -- the two
#     beats share both, so they can run back to back without double-posting.
#
# stdout (machine-parseable block the model echoes; sections best-effort):
#   ENTERED session_id=<id> exercise=<name> day=<code> slot=<i>/<n>
#     first_entry=<yes|no>
#   SET_TABLE delivered=<yes|no> ...   (the (2) table went to the owner as its
#                                       OWN message, sent by code. Nothing to
#                                       relay: the fence is on the owner's
#                                       screen, not on this stdout. Only a
#                                       FAILED send falls back to printing the
#                                       de-fenced rows here.)
#   EXERCISE_CARD ...                  (the (3) card lines)
#   PINNED_CARD written=<yes|no>       (표3 written to the dashboard.md pin
#                                       surface -> bridge auto-pins+syncs it)
#   CONFIRMED_SETTINGS ...             (grip/setup/loading -- one k=v per line)
#   RECORD_PARAMS ...                  (weak_side / unilateral order)
#   PREP_PLAN entry=<n> immediate_primer=<m>   (#10/#11/#26 F2 prep buckets)
#   PREP_ENTRY code=K1 phase=equipment_prep display="..."   (present at entry)
#   COOLDOWN_PLAN entry=<n>                    (2026-08-22 cooldown peer block;
#   COOLDOWN_ENTRY code=HP1 phase=cooldown ...  emitted only for a cooldown
#                                               drill pinned to THIS slot --
#                                               none today, so no line today)
#   PREP_IMMEDIATE defer=first_working_set code=K4 ...       (DEFER to just
#                                       before the first working set, not now)
#   ANCHOR prior=<N>kg ... note="직전 N kg -> 오늘 M kg"   (#43 prior-actual
#                                       anchor; first-ever -> note=첫 기록)
#   or ERROR <reason> on a hard arg failure only.
#
# Exit codes: 0 = entry handled (sections best-effort). 1 = bad args / missing
# files (a hard failure BEFORE any entry work).
#
# Reuse (ladder): set-table.render + find_day_and_slot (day/slot resolver +
# (2) table), rx-calc.load_yaml (stdlib YAML). stdlib only. ASCII source;
# Korean literals only where they are DB/program codes or user-visible cue
# prose (the settings/cues are Korean in program.yaml and shown verbatim).

